#: ../../../api/udf_decorators.md:1
msgid "UDF decorators"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/udf_decorators.md:3
msgid ""
"Each parameter states which integrations support it. **All integrations** "
"means xlwings Lite, xlwings Server, and classic xlwings on Windows (VBA "
"integration)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/udf_decorators.md:1
msgid "Registers a Python function as an Excel custom function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/udf_decorators.md:3
msgid ""
"Use `@xw.func` or `@xw.func(...)`. Function annotations describe argument "
"and return converters; {func}`arg <xlwings.arg>` and {func}`ret "
"<xlwings.ret>` provide explicit converter options. The function's docstring "
"supplies its description in Excel. Classic xlwings registers functions with "
"**Import Python UDFs**; xlwings Lite and xlwings Server register them when "
"the project is loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/udf_decorators.md:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlfunc:8
msgid ""
"**All integrations.** Function to decorate when calling "
"``func(my_function)`` directly. Leave it out when using ``@func`` or "
"``@func(...)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/udf_decorators.md:0
msgid "Keyword Arguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlfunc:11
msgid ""
"**xlwings Lite and xlwings Server only.** Excel-facing name, preserving the "
"supplied spelling. By default, Excel uses the uppercase Python function name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlfunc:12
msgid ""
"**xlwings Lite and xlwings Server only.** Function namespace, overriding the "
"module-level ``__xlwings_func_namespace__``. An empty string suppresses that "
"module-level namespace. A namespace configured in the add-in manifest is "
"prepended separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlfunc:13
msgid ""
"**All integrations.** Recalculate whenever Excel calculates. Defaults to "
"``False``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlfunc:14
msgid ""
"**xlwings Lite and xlwings Server only.** Cache custom-function results in "
"the add-in. Defaults to ``False``; cannot be combined with ``volatile=True`` "
"or a streaming function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlfunc:15
msgid ""
"**xlwings Lite and xlwings Server only.** URL shown as additional help in "
"Excel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.script:13 xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlfunc:16
msgid ""
"**xlwings Server only.** Roles required for a server-authenticated user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlfunc:17
msgid ""
"**Classic xlwings only.** Excel function category: a built-in category "
"number from 1 to 14 or a custom string. Defaults to ``\"xlwings\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlfunc:18
msgid ""
"**Classic xlwings only.** Whether to evaluate the function in Excel's "
"function wizard. Defaults to ``True``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlfunc:19
msgid ""
"**Classic xlwings only.** Set to ``\"threading\"`` to run an I/O-bound "
"function asynchronously. Defaults to ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/udf_decorators.md:0
msgid "Returns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.script:21 xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlfunc:21
msgid "The decorated function, or a decorator when called with options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/udf_decorators.md:0
msgid "Return type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.script:26 xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlarg:20
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlfunc:26 xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlret:18
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/udf_decorators.md:1
msgid "Registers a Python function as a runnable script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/udf_decorators.md:3
msgid ""
"Use `@xw.script` or `@xw.script(...)`. In xlwings Lite and xlwings Server, "
"exactly one parameter must be annotated with {class}`Book <xlwings.Book>` or "
"{class}`BookAsync <xlwings.BookAsync>` so the runtime can supply the "
"workbook. Use that parameter instead of constructing `xw.Book()`. In xlwings "
"Lite, `BookAsync` skips preloading cell values; define an `async def` script "
"and read values with `await rng.get_value()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/udf_decorators.md:5
msgid ""
"With classic xlwings, **Import Python UDFs** registers the script as a VBA "
"`Sub` procedure. The injected workbook parameter described above applies to "
"xlwings Lite and xlwings Server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.script:10
msgid ""
"**All integrations.** Function to decorate when calling "
"``script(my_function)`` directly. Leave it out when using ``@script`` or "
"``@script(...)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.script:12
msgid ""
"**xlwings Lite and xlwings Server only.** Display name of the script. "
"Defaults to the Python function name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.script:14
msgid ""
"**xlwings Lite and xlwings Server only.** Sheet name or list of names whose "
"content is loaded for the script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.script:15
msgid ""
"**xlwings Lite and xlwings Server only.** Sheet name or list of names whose "
"content is excluded from loading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.script:16
msgid ""
"**xlwings Lite and xlwings Server only.** Sheet-button reference, for "
"example ``\"[mybutton]Sheet1!A1\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.script:17
msgid ""
"**xlwings Lite and xlwings Server only.** Whether clicking the sheet button "
"opens the task pane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.script:19
msgid ""
"**All integrations.** Further options depend on the integration. Classic "
"xlwings supports ``category``, ``call_in_wizard``, ``volatile``, and "
"``async_mode``, as described under :func:`func <xlwings.func>`; xlwings Lite "
"and xlwings Server use them as additional script metadata. In xlwings Lite, "
"the legacy ``lazy`` option is deprecated; annotate the workbook parameter "
"with ``BookAsync`` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/udf_decorators.md:1
msgid "In xlwings Lite:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/udf_decorators.md:1
msgid "Sets the converter and options for a named custom-function argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/udf_decorators.md:3
msgid ""
"Place `@xw.arg(...)` below `@xw.func`. The argument name must match a Python "
"parameter. Converter options follow {meth}`Range.options "
"<xlwings.Range.options>`; `doc` supplies the argument description shown in "
"Excel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlarg:8
msgid "**All integrations.** Name of the Python parameter to configure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlarg:9
msgid ""
"**All integrations.** Converter, such as ``numpy.array`` or "
"``pandas.DataFrame``. Omit it to retain the argument's existing converter, "
"including one selected by a type annotation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlarg:11
msgid ""
"**All integrations.** Converter options, such as ``ndim=2``, "
"``index=False``, or ``header=False``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlarg:12
msgid "**All integrations.** Argument description shown in Excel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlarg:13
msgid ""
"**Classic xlwings only.** VBA expression that supplies a Python argument, "
"for example ``vba=\"Sheet1\"``. Excel supplies this argument by evaluating "
"the VBA expression, so users omit it from the worksheet formula."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlarg:15 xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlret:13
msgid ""
"A decorator that applies the configured conversion options to the function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/udf_decorators.md:1
msgid "Sets the converter and options for a custom function's return value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/udf_decorators.md:3
msgid ""
"Place `@xw.ret(...)` below `@xw.func`. Converter options follow {meth}"
"`Range.options <xlwings.Range.options>` and control how the Python result "
"becomes Excel cell values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlret:8
msgid ""
"**All integrations.** Return converter. Omit it to retain the existing "
"converter, including one selected by a type annotation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlret:10
msgid ""
"**All integrations.** Converter options, such as ``index=False`` and "
"``header=False`` for a DataFrame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/pro/udfs_officejs.py:docstring of
#: xlwings.pro.udfs_officejs.xlret:11
msgid ""
"**Classic xlwings only.** Set to ``\"table\"`` for legacy dynamic-array "
"expansion on Excel versions without native dynamic arrays. This overwrites "
"existing data and cannot take volatile formulas such as ``TODAY()`` as "
"arguments. Excel versions with native dynamic arrays, xlwings Lite, and "
"xlwings Server spill array results without this option."
msgstr ""
